What are Turbine Gear Boxes?
Turbine gear boxes are high torque planetary gear assemblies that bridge the speed gap between the slow turning wind turbine rotor and the fast turning generator. By stepping up the rotation speed, they enable generators to produce electricity efficiently across a wide range of wind speeds. Modern gear boxes are engineered to withstand fluctuating aerodynamic loads, torsional stresses, and, in offshore environments, corrosive saltwater exposure. Their reliability directly influences turbine availability and the overall levelised cost of energy (LCOE).
